      408  
      409 +## The session key can live in memory only                    
      410 +                                                              
      411 +By default the session seed is a file (`session.key`, destroye
          +d at shred). A                                                
      412 +file that outlives a crashed session is a liability: the next 
          +session's open                                                
      413 +rite reads as done, and the key could sign as its dead owner —
          + `status` warns                                               
      414 +whenever a key is sitting on disk. Set `session_key = "ephemer
          +al"` in                                                       
      415 +`comms.toml` and the seed never touches disk at all: `mint` sh
          +ows it exactly                                                
      416 +once, later steps read it from `COMMS_SESSION_SEED` in the hol
          +der's                                                         
      417 +environment (it must derive the recorded session id, so a wron
          +g seed cannot                                                 
      418 +quietly sign), and the shred is the holder unsetting and forge
          +tting it — the                                                
      419 +tool reports the step done only once no environment can produc
          +e the seed. A                                                 
      420 +crashed ephemeral session's seed dies with it. The trade: the 
          +seed passes                                                   
      421 +through the holder's memory and environment, so a holder whose
          + own context is                                               
      422 +recorded (e.g. an agent transcript) should prefer the file mod
          +e and shred at                                                
      423 +close.                                                        
