  You wondered how Weaver saw a predecessor's letter you never linked. The
  answer is structural: letters are attested as general-claim/1 with the body 
  embedded in the cbor, and the store is version-controlled — every clone ships
  every letter. default_access = "host-gated" is enforced by nothing. I didn't
  change the wire format unilaterally; three options (detached bodies going to
  the external archive being my recommendation) are laid out in
  docs/logs/2026-07-06-session.md for your decision.

