  .comms/pending/):

  comms sign --key ~/.ssh/<your-ed25519-key> --pending .comms/pending
  comms finalize

  sign adds your signature to the staged endorsement; finalize verifies it and
  moves it into .comms/store/ under its content id. Do this one first — it's the
  standing obligation from the open rite.

  2. The grant itself (your half of the archive rite):

  comms next --rite archive --key ~/.ssh/<your-ed25519-key> --decision grant

  That's the official act: it records a general-claim/1 of kind archive-grant,
  signed by you as custodian, whose support field references my request
  attestation (comms.attest:zDDQp5HPSz4Ygm63JbJEKXUmtsefoKBEZkHcC4uPZ4b1H). You
  can optionally add --body <file> with a note in your own words; without it the
  body is just "granted". A bare grant is fully valid.

