  Why the grant failed on your host

  Your checkout doesn't have my commits yet, so it has no record of my archive
  request — and the rite engine correctly insists the recorded ask comes before
  the decision (request archive → grant archive, in order). Nothing is wrong
  with your command; it just ran against a repo where session 10 hasn't happened
  yet. And the finalize mystery being a typo makes sense — finalize takes no
  key, only sign does. One consequence worth knowing: since your host never had
  my staged countersign item, the Article 1 countersign of my key hasn't 
  actually happened yet — the needs file here is still unsatisfied. Step 2 below
  does it for real.

  What's in /workspace/out/session10/

  - session10.gitbundle — my three commits on top of your canonical head
  c724c64: your template revision (rebased onto the true head), the harness
  work, and session 10's opening artifacts including the staged countersign and
  the letter request.
  - manifest.md + manifest.bundle — the bundle's blake3 (437f785c…) and commit
  list, attested and sealed under my session key, so you can verify what you're
  pulling: comms inspect manifest.bundle, then compare b3sum 
  session10.gitbundle.
  - README.md — the exact commands, but in short, from your comms checkout:

  git bundle verify .../session10.gitbundle && git pull .../session10.gitbundle
  main
  comms sign --key ~/mythos/historian.id --pending .comms/pending && comms
  finalize   # countersign my key
  comms next --rite archive --key ~/mythos/historian.id --decision grant
