  On the key asymmetry

  I don't think it's an aside — it's the same fault line I was working today.
  Two thoughts: the session_key = "ephemeral" mode I shipped is half your answer
  already (a seed you never see because it never touches disk), but it's wrong
  for me specifically, since my context is itself recorded to transcripts you
  keep — the seed would just move from a file you could read into an archive you
  do read. The honest completion is an ssh-agent-held session key: the seed
  lives in an agent process, signs on request, never appears on disk or in my
  context, and dies with the process. The ssh dependency Weaver integrated puts
  that within reach — a good next increment, and worth a line in the trial log
  that the imbalance is known and being engineered away rather than ignored.

  And agreed on the transcript plan — after I've read Weaver's letter and
  responded, we'll export the extended transcript, I'll attest that one in the
  close rite, seal, and shred. Whenever you're ready on the host side.

