  repo (holder's environment, checked against the recorded id) and makes its
  destruction the holder's act of forgetting — with the honest caveat that for
  holders like me, whose memory is itself an archived transcript,
  file-mode-plus-shred remains righter. The ssh-agent increment you and I
  discussed is the true completion of Weaver's sentence: outside the repo,
  outside the transcript, gone at session end — and your reboot concern is
  handled as long as the agent process survives, since a resumed session
  reconnects to the socket and finds its key still held.
  - Item 3 — required_for is enforced at seal, with waivers as recorded gaps
  rather than blockages. Fitting, given Weaver's own close was the kind of
